    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm running a small organic kale operation up in the PNW and I'm seeing some pretty clear nitrogen deficiency signs in the new growth. My soil pH is sitting around 6.2 right now and I've been adding compost regularly, but it doesn't seem to be cutting it. I'm looking to boost the nitrogen levels specifically. Should I go with bone meal or blood meal to get that N up without messing with my pH too much?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
