      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since you need a quick nitrogen boost, **blood meal** is generally a more immediate choice because it is much higher in readily available nitrogen compared to bone meal. While both will affect your soil in ways, blood meal is primarily a nitrogen source and will likely have a minimal impact on your current pH of 6.2. Apply it according to package directions and consider a light side-dressing application to target the new kale growth directly.",
      "source": "target",
